{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he uncovered himself.</b> A reflexive form." "<b>His tent.</b> Written אהלה — a hint to the ten tribes called after Shomron, which is called אָהֳלָה, for they were exiled on account of the matter of wine, as it says: ״הַשֹּׁתִים בְּמִזְרְקֵי יַיִן״ (Amos 6)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {1 "אהלה is written defectively (without the vav of אָהֳלָה), the shorter spelling yielding the numerical value ten — Rashi's hint to the ten tribes."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:10.374620833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}